1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
This video introduces the virtual model IK joint printing function for you.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
In this version, we have introduced the virtual model IK joint printing function.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
This function allows the virtual model to be imported from outside to be able to use the action and posture provided by Clo.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
So let's take a look at the IK joint printing function together.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,000
IK joint printing is currently only supported for FBX files with Google information.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,000
First, we need to import an FBX file to print the IK joint.

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Before importing, we need to explain some important things to note before printing IK.

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,000
FBX files should not have repeated name joints.

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:48,000
In addition, virtual models must include joints that include shoulders, elbows, wrists, pelvis, knees, and ankles.

10
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
T-position is the standard position for reference for IK printing.

11
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,000
IK printing with incorrect positioning may lead to errors.

12
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Therefore,

13
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,000
it is necessary to correctly set the virtual model as T-position.

14
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,000
If the virtual model is not T-position,

15
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,000
it is necessary to manually adjust the joint point of the virtual model in the 3D window to T-position.

16
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,000
In the virtual model information display in the 3D vertical menu bar,

17
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,000
open the virtual model joint point,

18
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,000
then press the joint point of the virtual model,

19
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:16,000
adjust the virtual model to T-position.

20
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,000
It is necessary to note that

21
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:22,000
for non-humanoid images or four animal virtual models in the structure,

22
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:24,000
IK printing may not be correctly applied.

23
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Now,

24
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,000
let us print the IK joint to the virtual model.

25
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,000
In the main menu bar,

26
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,000
find the virtual model editor under the virtual model,

27
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,000
then select the IK joint option card.

28
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Now our virtual model is already T-position.

29
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:39,000
Next,

30
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,000
press the set T-position in the upper right corner

31
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,000
to identify the adjusted T-position.

32
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:46,000
If the setting is completed according to the above operations,

33
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:49,000
the reset position button on the right will be activated.

34
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:52,000
After adjusting the position during the IK printing process,

35
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,000
the reset position button can help you restore the original position.

36
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Next,

37
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,000
let's print the joint.

38
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:59,000
There are two main ways to print the joint.

39
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:01,000
You can manually print each joint,

40
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:05,000
or you can automatically print the joint by identifying the name of the joint.

41
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,000
First,

42
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:09,000
let's see how to manually print the joint according to the joint list.

43
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Let's look at the joint list first.

44
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:14,000
The joint printing is divided into the required and the selected category.

45
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,000
The corresponding joint name is listed under the category.

46
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,000
To ensure that the IK joint printing is accurate,

47
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:21,000
you must print the desired type of IK joint.

48
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,000
For example,

49
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,000
you must print all the required parts,

50
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,000
but for the selected one,

51
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,000
although it is not a must-set,

52
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,000
if the virtual model has these joints,

53
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:34,000
you can print them to present more accurate movements and positions.

54
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Now,

55
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:38,000
let's carefully print the joints of the required project.

56
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:39,000
First,

57
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,000
when you click on the name of the joint,

58
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,000
you can check the preview on the top

59
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:46,000
to see which part of the selected joint is located in the virtual model.

60
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,000
You can also directly click on the joint in the preview

61
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,000
to find the corresponding position.

62
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,000
Next,

63
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:55,000
select the corresponding joint in the 3D window,

64
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,000
or you can first click on the joint in the virtual model,

65
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:01,000
then click on the project in the option card to print it.

66
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:04,000
I will print it from the top.

67
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:06,000
If multiple joints overlap,

68
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,000
you can choose which joint to print.

69
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:09,000
After printing,

70
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:12,000
the printing area will be displayed in the preview of the 3D window

71
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:16,000
and the virtual model editor in the green color.

72
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,000
In the joint list,

73
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:20,000
there will be a white contrast mark on the left side of the joint,

74
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:23,000
which indicates that the joint printing is complete.

75
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:24,000
In addition,

76
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,000
the name of the joint saved for the virtual model

77
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:29,000
will be displayed next to the printing box on the right.

78
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,000
If you misprinted the joint,

79
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:33,000
and want to re-select the joint to be printed,

80
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,000
you can select the joint in the joint list,

81
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:37,000
or the joint in the preview,

82
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:41,000
then click on another joint to re-print it.

83
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Or you can also select the image in the joint list,

84
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,000
or the joint in the preview,

85
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:49,000
then press the Delete key on the keyboard to delete it,

86
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:52,000
and then re-select the correct joint point.

87
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:53,000
Now,

88
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:55,000
let's pay attention to the remaining projects.

89
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:57,000
You can see that when printing the left joint,

90
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,000
the right one is also printed.

91
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:01,000
This is because the symmetrical printing

92
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:04,000
is not used in the upper right corner of the virtual model editor.

93
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:05,000
Therefore,

94
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,000
even if you print one side of the joint,

95
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:10,000
it will automatically identify and print the other side of the joint.

96
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,000
Please note that

97
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,000
if you want to automatically use symmetrical printing,

98
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:16,000
the joint name must be left and right,

99
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:18,000
or letters L and R or small letters L and R,

100
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:21,000
plus the bottom line is divided left and right.

101
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,000
You can select the joint point,

102
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:25,000
and then modify the name in the virtual editor.

103
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:27,000
If you do not open the symmetrical printing,

104
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:30,000
you need to manually print the left and right joints separately.

105
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:33,000
Now let's continue to print all the remaining joints below.

106
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Once all the joints of the required project are printed,

107
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:39,000
the state on the right side of the project will be displayed as complete,

108
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:42,000
indicating that the IK printing is complete.

109
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:45,000
Next, let's see how to automatically print the joints.

110
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Before automatically printing the joints,

111
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,000
let's press the reset button at the top,

112
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:51,000
to reset all the joints printed at the moment.

113
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:54,000
When you press the auto-print button at the bottom,

114
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:57,000
all the required joints under the required project will be automatically printed.

115
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:00,000
You can see that the state is also displayed as complete.

116
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,000
But what you need to pay attention to is that

117
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:03,000
only when the joint name of the virtual model

118
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:06,000
is the same as the joint name in the virtual model,

119
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:08,000
or the virtual model file is from

120
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:12,000
DeathMiximoCharacterCreator or MetaHuman,

121
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:15,000
the auto-printing function will work normally.

122
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:16,000
Next, let's take a look at

123
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:19,000
how to store the information of the IK joint printing.

124
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:22,000
The information of the IK joint printing of the virtual model

125
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,000
can be stored as an IKS file.

126
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:27,000
You can click on the save and open in the upper right corner,

127
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:31,000
and save the IK data as an IKS file,

128
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:35,000
or open the stored IKS file.

129
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,000
After completing all the joint printing,

130
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:40,000
you can directly apply the available posture.

131
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:41,000
What needs to be explained is that

132
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:44,000
IKS files only have the same structure,

133
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:47,000
and are integrated between the virtual models of the same printing method.

134
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:50,000
You can see that the posture has been correctly applied.

135
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:55,000
The virtual model file of the IK joint printing can be stored as the virtual model format that can be leaked.

136
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:57,000
Next time you can use it directly.

137
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:01,000
By using the new IK joint printing function in the virtual model editor,

138
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:06,000
you can more easily use various virtual models in the cloud to realize your design.

